{"t": 195.865, "n": 147, "ev": "result", "ok": true, "text": "I wrote the task rows for all five phases and the proof table into `docs/plans/i153.plan.md`. Nothing was run, since this step has no shell. The status is still `planned`, and sections 0, 1 and 4 and the goals are unchanged.\n\n- **Phase 1 (1.1–1.5):** three test rows come first, then the code rows in `nodes.py` and `council_run.py`.\n- **Phase 2 (2.1–2.3):** two test rows, then one code row for the judge side in `nodes.py`.\n- **Phase 3 (3.1–3.6):** two test rows, then code rows in `gate.py`, `nodes.py`, `status.py` and `detail.py`.\n- **Phase 4 (4.1–4.11):** three test rows, then code rows in `flow.py`, `gate.py`, `runner.py`, `nodes.py` and `council_run.py`. It also has three chore rows that regenerate the diagram of each workflow package (`temperspec-tgraph`, `release-notes-tgraph`, `doc-refresh-tgraph`).\n- **Phase 5 (5.1–5.2):** one docs row each for the running-workflows guide and `pauses.md`.\n- **Requirements:** every requirement R1–R7 is named by at least one row.\n- **Test ids:** the test rows carry the spec criterion ids, plus the task's `AC <n>` where noted.\n- **Verification:** the four commands were already in the plan and are allowed by `tempergraph.commands.json`, so I left them as they were. The proof table maps AC 1–8 to `tests/test_usage_limit.py` and its pytest command.\n\nJudgement calls and gaps:\n- **Judge route:** the plan has the human node route to `<unit>.judge`, so row 4.4 adds an edge to `human_targets`. That changes the diagram digest of the three workflow packages, and their self-test (`selftest.py`) fails on a stale digest. The chore rows 4.9–4.11 regenerate `diagram/model.json`; the same command rewrites each package's `workflow.md` and `stamp.json`. I did not open `stamp.json` or `workflow.md`, and I did not check that `tempergraph upgrade-check <workflow> --stamp` is the right command for `stamp.json`. It is the command the self-test message names.\n- **Rerun prompt inputs:** a rerun of a refused step has to rebuild the same prompt. The judge node overwrites the judgements, and the gate clears one-time feedback. Row 4.7 therefore has the refused record keep a `reuse` block of those inputs, and row 1.4 and its follow-up write it.\n- **Council reruns:** council member and chair sessions get their own rows (1.5, 4.8) because the council code reads a not-ok session as a missing answer.\n- **Not checked:** the hand-off lists `proceed` at a usage-limit pause as an open question. I left it accepted, as the plan says.\n- **Not committed:** I could not commit the plan, because the step forbids running git. The engine commits the file.\n\nARTIFACT phases: docs/plans/i153.plan.md", "subtype": "success", "is_error": false, "session_id": "40ac80b3-5d01-473a-a1a6-960261eef4ef"}
